{
    "background_story": "Lyra was a rare and majestic eel who lived in the depths of the ocean. Unlike her bony counterparts, Lyra's slender body was remarkably flexible, allowing her to slither through the tightest crevices in search of food. Her boneless physique also granted her an uncanny ability to absorb shocks and vibrations, making her a skilled hunter in the dark, pressurized waters. Lyra's unique characteristics made her a subject of fascination among the ocean's creatures, who would often gather to watch her glide effortlessly through the coral reef. Despite her ethereal appearance, Lyra was a formidable predator, using her agility and stealth to catch her prey off guard. Her boneless body became a symbol of adaptability and resilience in the ocean's ever-changing environment.",
